task:
Write a Ken program that:
1. for each customer computes the total number of items (`qty`), and then displays all results from the largest value to the smallest, in the format `customer - total`;
2. computes, for each category, the percentage of orders whose product name contains the fragment `lap` among all orders of that category, rounded to 1 decimal place, and then outputs the single entry with the smallest value (ascending), one per line in the format `category: X%`.

Write a Ken program that:
1. calculates the ratio of the total number of units (`units`) to the number of shipments for each result, considering only shipments from the month `2026-05`, rounded to 2 decimal places, and then prints alphabetically only the entries whose value is at least 6.3, in the format `result: ratio`;
2. classifies every one of the shipments by its value `units` × `unit_cost`: `low` if it is less than 50, `medium` if it is less than 222, and `high` otherwise. Print the number of shipments in each class, most numerous first, in the format `class: count`.

Write a Ken program that:
1. calculates the number of orders among orders where `price` is greater than 100 and prints just the value (first print the text `Overview:`);
2. computes the number of orders for each month, considering only orders whose product name contains the fragment `oe` and labels each result: `good` if it is at least 8 and `poor` otherwise, using your own word `bucket` for the rule. Print the labels chronologically by month, in the format `month - label`.

Write a Ken program that:
